// cross-module inlining, which the module system must not cost anything.
//
// Both callees live in modcore and both are called once from here. Under `-O` neither call may survive: the
// optimizer has to be able to see through a module boundary, or splitting a program into modules would be a
// performance decision rather than an organisational one.
echo modcore::tripled(14);
echo modcore::doubled(21);
